### New User Flow

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Upload CSV] --> B[Start Analysis]
    B --> C[DPSU profiles dataset]
    C --> D[QBII generates 3-5 questions]
    D --> E[User answers questions in UI]
    E --> F[QBII infers intent]
    F --> G[DRIL writes & runs repair script]
    G --> H[EPR writes & runs exploration script]
    H --> I[GAL fully populated]
```

### Key Design Decisions
- **No Docker**: Local `subprocess.run()` keeps it simple. Docker can be added later for ML model training.
- **Graceful fallback**: If a generated script fails, agents fall back to original data rather than crashing the pipeline.
- **Full traceability**: Every generated script is saved to `eva_sessions/<id>/scripts/` and its stdout/stderr is stored in the GAL.

